      "value": "@{60411ec5cc01c21febdcbe37|full_name}: VRChat doesn't have game servers, they do use a sort of server to connect everyone, but it is (if we simplify) jusy a fancy relay.\n\nWhen something changes in a world, the master of it (not nessessarily instance host) posts it to the relay server which distributes the changes to everyone else.\n\nFor this reason games like table tennis basically doesn't work at all, because physics can only be calculated by one person and then has to be streamed over.\n\nSo right now, if you want good physics then you need to be able to easily define who will calculate it and how it could be cleanly shifted over to someone else, in the case of two players touching each other it will mess up a ton, as you need both to calculate their own, so physics will be delayed by the combination of their delays, because we would need to do a round trip.\n\nSo if the both of you are barely moving or are taking turns moving then it would work, but the moment you both are moving you would definitely notice the delay, which personally would absolutely break my immersion.\n\nAnd therefore I think your world collision idea is fine (although it is yet another thing the dinky Quest processor would have to deal with, so would probably have to be world cap limited). However your player on player physics I believe will just be messy, VRChat just has too much latency for it.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
