      "value": "@{60411ec5cc01c21febdcbe37|full_name}: https://docs.vrchat.com/docs/vrchat-202231p2#fixes would seem like they did completely disable avatar haptics on Quest.\n\nAlso, it is actually related because the reason why they did it as they did was because doing full on collision calculations would be too much for Quest, behind the scenes doing avatar haptics and full on physics like you want would require the same thing, a way to detect the mesh.\n\nWhile they could do it the way Bonelab's does it, that would require **every single avatar** to be reuploaded with it setup, because automated systems would not only be very annoying to develop, but would likely also produce terrible collisions meshes.\n\nIn the end however, the biggest reason why I highly doubt this would be added as you want it, is because most people cannot handle boneworks or bonelab's without getting motion sick. Forcing movement on someone is literally rule 1 of what you shouldn't do in a VR game.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
