      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{61d4c34e9b9a8309bf0dc512|full_name}: But unfortunately VRChat doesn't really have servers, it is a sort of p2p network where everything is run through a relay server (so you do not expose your IP address and it scales way better than if it was actually p2p).\n\nMy guess is that it works like this; any network event is posted to the relay server, this is then distributed to everyone else. All physics calculation and other networked event has a master (usually the person who last interacted with it) who does the calculations locally and then posts them to the relay.\n\nSo as VRChat works right now, this couldn't work.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
