      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5c2f5434e10cd7317fce9d5c|full_name}: True you are right, although that is still a server just, as you said, is only really responsible for people’s connection to the instance and getting their information securely to everyone else. But this does mean they have something there and wouldn’t need to transition away from p2p for the server to start doing some of the heavy lifting, which means it is possible without rewriting everything, you could even allow udon to work properly by making it so anytime it calls to set the instance owner it just makes it the server, but you are still right. While it would be easier then turning a p2p system into a server setup, it would still take a monumental amount of time and effort to do.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
