      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{61d4c34e9b9a8309bf0dc512|full_name}: VRChat seems to use Photon for their networking, which means they probably do not have their own servers and I am only saying probably because the \"On Premise\" servers still require you to pay for licences and are apparently a bad deal compared to their cloud offering.\n\nSo yeah, I guess VRChat could have their own servers, but I highly doubt they would want to actually do any processing on them, if they did then I doubt you'd be able to mod the SDK to get around limits and the stated reason for why \"Texture Memory\" limiting still isn't a thing is because it can only be counted when an avatar has loaded in, which wouldn't be a problem if they just had a server do a simple check on the avatar.\n\nHowever, it would be very costly, which is why I highly doubt VRChat would do it.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
